  "notes": [
    "Reflexive -IR verb with an e→i stem change, following the same pattern as *vestirse*. The stem change appears in the presente (all but nosotros/nosotras), the 3rd-person forms of pretérito indefinido (se desvistió, se desvistieron), and throughout the subjuntivo presente — including nosotros/nosotras (nos desvistamos), since e→i type -IR stem-changers keep the change in that form.",
    "Past participle is regular: **desvestido**.",
    "Imperativo afirmativo reflexive pronouns attach to the end with a written accent to preserve stress (desvístete, desvístase, desvistámonos, desvístanse); imperativo negativo places them separately in front (no te desvistas...).",
    "*Se desvistió rápidamente antes de la ducha.* (\"He/she undressed quickly before the shower.\")",
    "*Los niños se desvisten solos antes de bañarse.* (\"The kids undress themselves before bathing.\")",
    "Related: *vestirse* (reflexive, \"to get dressed\" — antonym, same e→i pattern), *desvestir* (non-reflexive, \"to undress someone else\"), *la ropa* (clothes)."
  ],
